好吧，你们说说看，这难道不是你们收到过的最刻薄的邮件吗？

343
00:12:20.900 --> 00:12:21.260
Read it.
读出来。

344
00:12:21.260 --> 00:12:22.260
This is because I skipped a week.
这是因为我断了一周没学。

345
00:12:22.320 --> 00:12:23.480
I skipped a week.
我断了一周。

346
00:12:23.600 --> 00:12:25.560
This is because I skipped a week in Duolingo.
这是因为我在多邻国断了一周没学。

347
00:12:25.820 --> 00:12:26.900
Okay, what does it say?
好吧，上面写了什么？

348
00:12:26.960 --> 00:12:27.420
Read it out loud.
大声读出来。

349
00:12:27.760 --> 00:12:30.380
How do you say quitter in Spanish?
“逃兵”用西班牙语怎么说？

350
00:12:30.660 --> 00:12:31.760
Yeah, that's the header of the email.
没错，这就是邮件的标题。

351
00:12:31.860 --> 00:12:32.940
How hostile is that?
这得多大敌意啊？

352
00:12:32.980 --> 00:12:34.240
And I like that you wrote back.
而且我很高兴你回信了。

353
00:12:34.300 --> 00:12:35.360
Sorry, that was harsh.
抱歉，刚才那话太刻薄了。

354
00:12:35.480 --> 00:12:36.060
No, that's them.
不，那是他们发的。

355
00:12:36.120 --> 00:12:37.180
That's the body of the email.
那是邮件的正文内容。

356
00:12:37.180 --> 00:12:40.020
Well, yeah, that's Duolingo texting me, yeah.
嗯，对，那是多邻国发给我的短信，没错。

357
00:12:40.420 --> 00:12:41.280
Oh, my gosh.
天哪。

358
00:12:41.280 --> 00:12:44.860
So, no, I don't speak another language, and Duolingo won't let me forget that.
所以，不，我不会说外语，而多邻国绝不会让我忘了这一点。

359
00:12:45.120 --> 00:12:45.600
Wow.
哇。

360
00:12:46.340 --> 00:12:50.620
Number three, what's a place you've been to that you loved?
第三个问题，你去过什么地方是你特别喜欢的？

361
00:12:50.760 --> 00:12:54.740
I just went to Brussels in November and went to Bruges.
我十一月刚去了布鲁塞尔，还去了布鲁日。

362
00:12:54.800 --> 00:12:55.900
I remember you talking about those.
我记得你提起过那些地方。

363
00:12:56.000 --> 00:12:56.320
And it was perfect.
那里简直完美。

364
00:12:56.500 --> 00:12:59.380
It was little cobblestone streets, and it was perfect.
到处是鹅卵石铺成的小路，一切都太完美了。

365
00:12:59.380 --> 00:12:59.960
I love it.
我喜欢那里。

366
00:13:00.200 --> 00:13:00.880
Love that.
我也喜欢。

367
00:13:00.880 --> 00:13:04.000
And what do you like to do on the weekends?
那你周末喜欢做什么？

368
00:13:04.380 --> 00:13:09.700
On the weekends, you can usually find me at music festivals volunteering with End Overdose.
周末的话，你通常能在音乐节上找到我，我在为“终结过量”（End Overdose）做志愿者。

369
00:13:09.840 --> 00:13:16.140
It's a group that gives out Narcan for reversing opioid overdoses, and just trying to get the information out.
这是一个发放纳洛酮以逆转阿片类药物过量的组织，我们只是努力把这些信息传播出去。

370
00:13:16.800 --> 00:13:23.160
I always see you post about that, and you just have such a heart for others, and I just love that about you so much.
我总能看到你发关于这个的内容，你真的很有爱心，我特别欣赏你这一点。

371
00:13:23.600 --> 00:13:26.500
Okay, last question from the call sheet.
好了，提纲上的最后一个问题。

372
00:13:26.960 --> 00:13:28.600
Favorite midnight snack?
最喜欢的宵夜是什么？

373
00:13:28.800 --> 00:13:30.640
Midnight snack would be Indian food.
宵夜的话，我会选印度菜。

374
00:13:30.880 --> 00:13:31.420
Oh, yeah?
哦，真的吗？

375
00:13:31.660 --> 00:13:32.460
At midnight?
在半夜吃？

376
00:13:32.700 --> 00:13:32.800
Yeah.
对。

377
00:13:32.800 --> 00:13:33.620
What specifically?
具体是什么？

378
00:13:33.960 --> 00:13:35.500
How do you sleep well?
那你怎么睡得着？

379
00:13:35.940 --> 00:13:35.990
I don't.
我睡不着。

380
00:13:36.000 --> 00:13:36.780
I sleep.
我只是在睡觉而已。

381
00:13:36.900 --> 00:13:40.260
My sleep schedule is horrific, and I'm aware these two are related.
我的作息时间糟透了，我知道这两者是有联系的。

382
00:13:40.520 --> 00:13:44.160
Do Indian food digesting in your stomach at midnight?
半夜吃印度菜在胃里消化，你受得了吗？

383
00:13:44.560 --> 00:13:46.980
I'll get up and have Indian food delivered.
我会起床点印度外卖。

384
00:13:47.080 --> 00:13:48.420
It'll get there at one in the morning.
凌晨一点送到。

385
00:13:48.640 --> 00:13:49.420
Oh, my gosh.
天哪。

386
00:13:50.300 --> 00:13:50.500
Yep.
没错。

387
00:13:50.780 --> 00:13:51.140
It's brutal.
太残暴了。

388
00:13:51.260 --> 00:13:52.680
Does it put you back to sleep?
吃完能让你重新入睡吗？

389
00:13:52.900 --> 00:13:53.380
Eventually.
最终能吧。

390
00:13:54.280 --> 00:13:54.760
Okay.
好吧。

391
00:13:55.100 --> 00:13:56.500
But no, it's definitely an upper.
但说真的，这绝对会让人兴奋。

392
00:13:56.780 --> 00:13:58.400
That I was not expecting.
这一点我真没想到。

393
00:13:58.400 --> 00:13:59.320
I wasn't either.
我也没想到。

394
00:13:59.320 --> 00:14:03.640
I was going to say cereal, but lamb, tiki, marsala?
我本来想说麦片，结果你说的是羊肉玛莎拉咖喱？

395
00:14:03.880 --> 00:14:04.040
Yeah.
对。

396
00:14:04.780 --> 00:14:05.260
All right.
好吧。

397
00:14:05.940 --> 00:14:18.860
I want to share one of my favorite behind the scenes with you, Sam, is early on when we would edit episodes, Angela and I would come in together with our notes,
Sam，我想和你分享一个我最喜欢的幕后故事，早期我们剪辑剧集的时候，Angela和我总是带着笔记一起过来，

398
00:14:18.860 --> 00:14:24.720
with our little sack lunches, and we would all cram into your editing day.
带着我们的小午餐袋，然后我们全都挤进你的剪辑室里。

399
00:14:24.720 --> 00:14:24.980
That's right.
没错。

400
00:14:25.180 --> 00:14:25.340
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

401
00:14:25.480 --> 00:14:32.660
And those few hours on those days are just some of my favorite memories from doing this podcaSt.
那些日子里的那几个小时，是我做这个播客以来最美好的回忆。

402
00:14:32.760 --> 00:14:33.640
Honestly, mine too.
说实话，我也是。

403
00:14:33.840 --> 00:14:34.080
Yeah.
没错。

404
00:14:34.220 --> 00:14:35.140
We would laugh.
我们会大笑。

405
00:14:35.320 --> 00:14:35.460
Yeah.
是啊。

406
00:14:35.460 --> 00:14:40.980
And we would laugh so hard, and we would be, you know, there was no extra tables.
我们会笑得前仰后合，而且你知道，当时根本没有多余的桌子。

407
00:14:41.300 --> 00:14:42.940
One time, there wasn't even enough chairs.
有一次，连椅子都不够。

408
00:14:43.080 --> 00:14:43.160
No.
没错。

409
00:14:43.160 --> 00:14:50.940
One of us was on the floor, and it kind of reminded me of those early days in, like, college where you all hung out in, like, someone's dorm room.
我们中有一个人坐在地板上，这让我想起了大学早期的日子，大家挤在某个人的宿舍里消磨时光。

410
00:14:51.000 --> 00:14:51.420
Mm-hmm.
嗯。

411
00:14:51.580 --> 00:14:55.160
We would eat our lunches in our laps, whatever they were.
我们把午餐放在膝盖上吃，不管吃的是什么。

412
00:14:55.260 --> 00:14:57.620
We had to balance them in our laps, plus our notes.
我们得在膝盖上保持平衡，还要放着笔记。

413
00:14:57.840 --> 00:14:58.160
Yeah.
是啊。

414
00:14:58.280 --> 00:15:01.440
And we were in a room that was, I don't know.
而且我们待的那个房间，怎么说呢。

415
00:15:01.580 --> 00:15:04.460
It was the size of a very small walk-in closet.
大概就只有一个很小的步入式衣帽间那么大。

416
00:15:04.460 --> 00:15:04.760
Yeah.
没错。

417
00:15:04.960 --> 00:15:05.140
Yeah.
是啊。

418
00:15:05.220 --> 00:15:06.120
And it was freezing.
而且冷得要命。

419
00:15:06.440 --> 00:15:06.580
Yes.
没错。

420
00:15:06.860 --> 00:15:07.080
Freezing.
冷极了。

421
00:15:07.380 --> 00:15:08.160
Yes, Earwolf was freezing.
是的，Earwolf 那里冷得要命。

422
00:15:08.160 --> 00:15:11.820
We have many photos of me and Angela in, like, full winter gear.
我们有很多照片，我和安吉拉穿着全套冬装。

423
00:15:12.000 --> 00:15:12.050
Yes.
没错。

424
00:15:12.080 --> 00:15:14.580
Yep, and, like, hoodies and beanies and stuff.
是啊，还有连帽衫、毛线帽之类的东西。

425
00:15:14.640 --> 00:15:14.980
Yeah.
没错。

426
00:15:15.340 --> 00:15:15.960
And mittens.
还有连指手套。

427
00:15:16.200 --> 00:15:20.760
But, you know, that was before the pandemic, before everybody discovered Zoom.
但你知道，那是在疫情之前，在大家发现 Zoom 之前。

428
00:15:20.940 --> 00:15:22.080
Now we edit on Zoom.
现在我们都在 Zoom 上剪辑了。

429
00:15:22.220 --> 00:15:24.060
But, man, I miss those times.
但是，天哪，我真怀念那些时光。

430
00:15:24.060 --> 00:15:26.800
And that was, you guys changed up, like, how a lot of us edited.
而且你们改变了我们很多人剪辑的方式。

431
00:15:27.260 --> 00:15:30.460
Up until then, podcasts, we just pretty much recorded.
在那之前，播客基本上就是录完就行。

432
00:15:30.660 --> 00:15:33.320
And there was, I don't know, two or three edits, and we'd turn them around.
大概也就两三次剪辑，然后就发布了。

433
00:15:33.320 --> 00:15:34.820
It was a pretty quick process.
那是一个相当快速的过程。

434
00:15:35.060 --> 00:15:38.380
But this show, like, really changed the way a lot of us edit at Earwolf.
但这个节目确实改变了我们很多 Earwolf 员工的剪辑方式。

435
00:15:38.820 --> 00:15:39.060
Wow.
哇。

436
00:15:39.500 --> 00:15:40.180
It was cool.
那真的很酷。

437
00:15:40.200 --> 00:15:42.120
Because we would edit in real time with you.
因为我们会和你实时进行剪辑。

438
00:15:42.240 --> 00:15:44.620
We tried emailing you notes and thoughts.
我们试过通过邮件发给你笔记和想法。

439
00:15:44.780 --> 00:15:46.180
And it was just, like, a mess.
结果简直是一团糟。

440
00:15:46.180 --> 00:15:48.340
Yeah, it just worked better for you to go put this here and point at it.
是啊，还是你直接过来把东西放在这儿指出来效果更好。

441
00:15:48.380 --> 00:15:48.780
Yeah.
没错。

442
00:15:49.080 --> 00:15:49.240
Yeah.
是啊。

443
00:15:50.220 --> 00:15:51.180
Aw, Sam.
噢，萨姆。

444
00:15:51.680 --> 00:15:54.180
Thank you so much for being on our 200th episode.
非常感谢你能来参加我们的第 200 期节目。

445
00:15:54.240 --> 00:15:57.580
And thank you for everything you've done for Office Ladies.
也感谢你为《办公室女士》所做的一切。

446
00:15:57.580 --> 00:16:05.700
And for everybody who has not listened to Sam's podcast, Enemy in Paris, you need to check it out.
对于还没听过萨姆播客《巴黎之敌》的朋友，你们一定要去听听。

447
00:16:05.800 --> 00:16:09.660
It is my new favorite, like, it's hilarious.
这是我最喜欢的新节目，太搞笑了。

448
00:16:10.200 --> 00:16:10.320
Re-watch podcaSt.
重温播客。

449
00:16:10.560 --> 00:16:10.860
Yes.
没错。

450
00:16:10.860 --> 00:16:19.880
And, you know, I was telling you before we started recording that I have not been re-watching the episodes because you guys do such a good job of describing them.
而且，你知道，我在录制前就跟你说过，我一直没在重温那些剧集，因为你们描述得太棒了。

451
00:16:19.980 --> 00:16:23.220
Oh, well, that's the goal is we don't want anyone to have to watch the show, ideally.
噢，好吧，我们的目标是理想情况下不希望任何人非得看这部剧。

452
00:16:23.560 --> 00:16:24.840
You don't want to have to watch it again.
你不需要非得再看一遍。

453
00:16:25.080 --> 00:16:25.300
Yeah.
没错。

454
00:16:25.300 --> 00:16:26.560
That is hilarious.
那太搞笑了。

455
00:16:26.560 --> 00:16:34.220
But it is, if you love to hate-watch Emily in Paris like we do, and we would always talk about it, this is the podcast for you.
但确实，如果你像我们一样喜欢一边吐槽一边看《艾米丽在巴黎》，而且我们总是讨论它，那么这就是适合你的播客。

456
00:16:34.520 --> 00:16:34.620
Yeah.
没错。

457
00:16:35.780 --> 00:16:37.980
But I love your opening song.
但我很喜欢你们的开场曲。

458
00:16:38.180 --> 00:16:40.020
I love how you guys describe the scenes.
我很喜欢你们描述场景的方式。

459
00:16:40.180 --> 00:16:41.840
I love your deep dives.
我很喜欢你们的深度解析。

460
00:16:42.140 --> 00:16:42.560
Uh-huh.
嗯哼。

461
00:16:42.700 --> 00:16:43.160
I-
我——

462
00:16:43.160 --> 00:16:44.840
Which are heavily lifted from this show.
那些内容很大程度上都是从这部剧里直接搬过来的。

463
00:16:44.980 --> 00:16:45.780
Oh, my gosh.
天哪。

464
00:16:46.000 --> 00:16:47.680
I mean, you guys are very entertaining.
我是说，你们真的很风趣。

465
00:16:48.040 --> 00:16:49.360
I love your co-hoSt.
我很喜欢你们的联合主持人。

466
00:16:49.820 --> 00:16:50.340
It's great.
太棒了。

467
00:16:50.640 --> 00:16:50.690
Yep, thank you.
是的，谢谢你。

468
00:16:50.690 --> 00:16:51.740
Everybody, go listen to it.
大家快去听听看。

469
00:16:51.760 --> 00:16:52.440
Go listen to it.
快去听听看。

470
00:16:55.300 --> 00:16:56.480
Sam also brought us-
萨姆还给我们带来了——

471
00:16:57.040 --> 00:16:59.680
Yes, I brought you guys so we have official merch.
是的，我给你们带了礼物，我们有官方周边了。

472
00:17:00.220 --> 00:17:06.980
There's an episode where this woman, this American actress, comes to Paris and only refers to Emily as Bucket Hat.
有一集里，有个女人，那个美国女演员，来到巴黎，只管艾米丽叫“渔夫帽”。

473
00:17:07.160 --> 00:17:07.340
Yes.
没错。

474
00:17:07.440 --> 00:17:10.760
And says, Bonsoir Bucket Hats, so we have Bonsoir Bucket Hats.
她说“晚上好，渔夫帽们”，所以我们印了“晚上好，渔夫帽们”。

475
00:17:10.880 --> 00:17:11.400
It's perfect.
太完美了。

476
00:17:11.680 --> 00:17:12.680
I love it so much.
我太喜欢了。

477
00:17:12.700 --> 00:17:13.840
I can't wait to wear it.
我迫不及待想穿上它了。

478
00:17:13.960 --> 00:17:15.220
I'm going to wear it on my walks.
我要穿着它去散步。

479
00:17:15.220 --> 00:17:16.320
I'm going to wear it on my hike.
我要穿着它去徒步。

480
00:17:16.460 --> 00:17:18.160
I'm going to take a picture of us in it, Jenna.
珍娜，我要拍一张我们穿着它的合影。

481
00:17:18.300 --> 00:17:18.520
Great.
太棒了。

482
00:17:20.920 --> 00:17:25.740
And I just wanted to say, my time here triggered something very special inside me.
我只想说，我在这里的时光在我内心深处触发了一些非常特别的东西。

483
00:17:25.860 --> 00:17:34.040
You two took a very simple concept of a recap show and made something extremely special, something extremely rare, something that bonds people.
你们俩把一个简单的重温节目的概念，做成了极其特别、极其罕见、能把人们凝聚在一起的东西。

484
00:17:34.320 --> 00:17:39.380
That's the thing that all podcast companies desperately want, that they foam at the mouth over, that they can't recreate.
这正是所有播客公司梦寐以求、垂涎三尺却又无法复制的东西。

485
00:17:39.660 --> 00:17:42.300
And it comes down to the people making it, the time it was made.
这归功于制作它的人，以及它诞生的那个时机。

486
00:17:42.480 --> 00:17:46.220
It takes a very special type of magic to create a show like this, and you two did it.
创造这样一个节目需要一种非常特殊的魔力，而你们俩做到了。

487
00:17:46.220 --> 00:17:48.220
I hope you're very proud of yourselves.
我希望你们能为自己感到非常骄傲。

488
00:17:48.420 --> 00:17:51.780
And if you ever doubt that, take a peek into the fan page on Facebook.
如果你们对此有任何怀疑，去看看Facebook上的粉丝专页吧。

489
00:17:51.960 --> 00:17:56.860
The community that has rallied behind this podcast is truly incredible and rare and magical.
这个支持播客的社区真的是不可思议、罕见且充满魔力的。

490
00:17:57.140 --> 00:18:01.380
And to that fandom, I just want to say you are seen and you are heard and you are loved.
对于那个粉丝群体，我只想说，你们被看见了，被听见了，也被爱着。

491
00:18:01.520 --> 00:18:04.180
Even when you think nobody sees you, you are seen and you are loved.
即使当你觉得没人注意到你时，你依然被看见，被爱着。

492
00:18:08.030 --> 00:18:11.490
I'm just, I don't know how to do the podcast without you.
我只是……我不知道没有你我该怎么做这个播客。

493
00:18:11.870 --> 00:18:12.730
It'll be okay.
一切都会好起来的。

494
00:18:14.940 --> 00:18:17.820
Sam, thank you so much for sharing that.
萨姆，非常感谢你的分享。

495
00:18:17.820 --> 00:18:26.080
But more than that, just thank you for believing in Jenna and I when we had so much self-doubt and we were in a whole new space.
但更重要的是，谢谢你在我们充满自我怀疑、身处全新领域时，依然相信我和珍娜。

496
00:18:26.260 --> 00:18:30.420
And some people wrote us off right away and you never did.
有些人一开始就否定了我们，但你从未这样做。

497
00:18:30.620 --> 00:18:30.920
Oh, no.
噢，不。

498
00:18:31.020 --> 00:18:33.060
You guys had something special right out of the gate.
你们从一开始就拥有一些特别的东西。

499
00:18:33.100 --> 00:18:34.840
And we just love you.
我们真的很爱你。

