嗯哼。

830
00:31:24.180 --> 00:31:26.360
Even though that is the backdrop for it.
尽管那是它的背景设定。

831
00:31:26.880 --> 00:31:27.260
Okay.
好吧。

832
00:31:28.020 --> 00:31:30.040
Cassie, Jordan, Eduardo?
卡西、乔丹、爱德华多？

833
00:31:31.520 --> 00:31:32.340
This is Jordan.
我是乔丹。

834
00:31:33.060 --> 00:31:35.560
I do not think it's a Christmas movie.
我不认为它是圣诞电影。

835
00:31:35.700 --> 00:31:36.020
Okay.
好吧。

836
00:31:36.340 --> 00:31:38.380
It is absolutely a Christmas movie.
它绝对是圣诞电影。

837
00:31:38.380 --> 00:31:39.540
Oh, my God, Eduardo.
天哪，爱德华多。

838
00:31:40.000 --> 00:31:40.720
Oh, Eduardo coming in hot.
噢，爱德华多态度很坚决啊。

839
00:31:40.820 --> 00:31:41.120
Okay.
好吧。

840
00:31:41.320 --> 00:31:41.800
Cassie?
卡西呢？

841
00:31:42.320 --> 00:31:45.220
Just because it's around Christmas doesn't make it a Christmas movie.
仅仅因为它发生在圣诞节期间，并不代表它就是圣诞电影。

842
00:31:45.220 --> 00:31:46.500
Thank you, Cassie.
谢谢你，卡西。

843
00:31:46.640 --> 00:31:48.040
Thank you, Cassie.
谢谢你，卡西。

844
00:31:48.160 --> 00:31:48.920
I feel seen.
我感觉被理解了。

845
00:31:49.160 --> 00:31:56.380
Eduardo, let me just say, at Christmas, I get inspired to watch Die Hard, so I'm going
爱德华多，我只想说，每到圣诞节，我都会受到启发去看《虎胆龙威》，所以我

846
00:31:56.380 --> 00:31:58.660
to put it as, yes, a Christmas movie.
把它归为圣诞电影，投赞成票。

847
00:31:58.980 --> 00:32:00.680
All right, it's three to two.
好吧，现在是三比二。

848
00:32:00.680 --> 00:32:10.240
In December 2023, Yahoo News, YouGov did a poll, and 50% of the people polled said no.
2023年12月，雅虎新闻和YouGov做了一项民意调查，50%的受访者表示不是。

849
00:32:11.200 --> 00:32:13.280
26% said yes.
26%的人表示是。

850
00:32:13.520 --> 00:32:13.740
Okay.
好吧。

851
00:32:14.100 --> 00:32:16.020
23% said they aren't sure.
23%的人表示他们不确定。

852
00:32:16.340 --> 00:32:16.820
Okay.
好吧。

853
00:32:16.820 --> 00:32:21.880
And only 14% of people said that they watch it over the holidays.
只有14%的人表示他们会在假期观看。

854
00:32:22.580 --> 00:32:29.800
Well, Yahoo UK had an article, and they have some criteria for whether or not something is
雅虎英国站曾发表过一篇文章，他们列出了一些标准，用来判断某部电影是否为

855
00:32:29.800 --> 00:32:30.720
a Christmas movie.
圣诞电影。

856
00:32:30.740 --> 00:32:36.600
And they said you can figure out if something is a Christmas movie by asking these two questions.
他们说，你可以通过问这两个问题来判断某部电影是否属于圣诞电影。

857
00:32:36.900 --> 00:32:38.080
I'm so curious.
我太好奇了。

858
00:32:38.600 --> 00:32:44.220
Number one, does watching the film at any other time of year feel weird?
第一，在一年中的其他时间观看这部电影会觉得奇怪吗？

859
00:32:44.820 --> 00:32:48.920
If the answer is no, then it is not a Christmas movie.
如果答案是否定的，那它就不是圣诞电影。

860
00:32:49.060 --> 00:32:49.940
I mean, the answer is no for me.
我的意思是，对我来说答案是否定的。

861
00:32:50.080 --> 00:32:51.600
I could watch Die Hard any time.
我随时都可以看《虎胆龙威》。

862
00:32:51.960 --> 00:32:52.220
Right.
没错。

863
00:32:52.380 --> 00:32:55.280
But for example, you probably wouldn't watch...
但举个例子，你可能不会看……

864
00:32:55.280 --> 00:32:56.720
Christmas Vacation.
《疯狂圣诞假期》。

865
00:32:56.900 --> 00:32:57.300
Yes.
是的。

866
00:32:57.520 --> 00:32:57.700
Right.
没错。

867
00:32:58.040 --> 00:33:00.320
But what about the movie Home Alone?
那《小鬼当家》呢？

868
00:33:00.880 --> 00:33:02.620
Is that a Christmas movie?
那是圣诞电影吗？

869
00:33:02.900 --> 00:33:04.340
I mean, I think so.
我觉得算是吧。

870
00:33:04.880 --> 00:33:07.560
But it's also just a comedy.
但它也只是一部喜剧片。

871
00:33:07.560 --> 00:33:09.260
Couldn't you watch that in the summer?
难道你不能在夏天看吗？

872
00:33:09.720 --> 00:33:11.680
And it's about a kid who's home alone?
而且讲的是一个孩子独自在家？

873
00:33:11.880 --> 00:33:12.440
You think...
你觉得……

874
00:33:12.440 --> 00:33:12.980
I don't know.
我不知道。

875
00:33:13.060 --> 00:33:13.600
It's winter.
那是冬天。

876
00:33:13.780 --> 00:33:14.560
There's snow everywhere.
到处都是雪。

877
00:33:15.060 --> 00:33:16.300
Planes, trains, and automobiles?
《飞机、火车和汽车》呢？

878
00:33:16.900 --> 00:33:18.440
I could watch that any time.
我随时都能看那部片子。

879
00:33:18.920 --> 00:33:19.200
Okay.
好吧。

880
00:33:19.700 --> 00:33:20.160
All right.
行吧。

881
00:33:20.160 --> 00:33:21.280
Here's the second question.
这是第二个问题。

882
00:33:21.620 --> 00:33:26.040
If you take Christmas out of the movie, does it still make sense?
如果把圣诞节元素从电影中剔除，它还讲得通吗？

883
00:33:26.460 --> 00:33:30.000
If the answer is yes, it's not a Christmas movie.
如果答案是肯定的，那它就不是圣诞电影。

884
00:33:30.220 --> 00:33:31.080
That's a good one.
这个标准不错。

885
00:33:31.180 --> 00:33:31.980
That's a good question.
这是个好问题。

886
00:33:32.280 --> 00:33:36.940
I think you could take Christmas out of Die Hard, and it's still Die Hard.
我觉得你可以把《虎胆龙威》里的圣诞元素去掉，它依然是《虎胆龙威》。

887
00:33:37.040 --> 00:33:37.360
Yes.
是的。

888
00:33:37.560 --> 00:33:42.260
So there's a lot of evidence here now that Die Hard is not a Christmas movie.
所以现在有很多证据表明《虎胆龙威》不是圣诞电影。

889
00:33:42.800 --> 00:33:48.700
I will tell you that Die Hard director John McTiernan spoke at the American Film Institute
我要告诉你，《虎胆龙威》的导演约翰·麦克蒂尔南曾在2020年美国电影学会上

890
00:33:48.700 --> 00:33:52.140
in 2020, and here's what he had to say.
发表过讲话，他是这么说的。

891
00:33:52.260 --> 00:33:58.580
He said, we hadn't intended it to be a Christmas movie, but the joy that came from it is what
他说，我们本来没打算把它拍成圣诞电影，但由此产生的欢乐氛围却

892
00:33:58.580 --> 00:34:00.680
turned it into a Christmas movie.
让它变成了一部圣诞电影。

893
00:34:01.940 --> 00:34:05.820
So John McTiernan says, yes, it's a Christmas movie.
所以约翰·麦克蒂尔南说，是的，它是圣诞电影。

894
00:34:06.100 --> 00:34:07.660
I don't know if he said yes.
我不知道他是否真的说了“是”。

895
00:34:07.660 --> 00:34:12.980
I think he just likes that people have attached this sort of debate to it and the fun of it.
我觉得他只是乐见人们围绕这部电影展开这种争论，并享受其中的乐趣。

896
00:34:12.980 --> 00:34:19.240
Well, I think the ultimate authority on whether or not this is a Christmas movie is Bruce Willis, right?
嗯，我觉得判断这到底是不是圣诞电影的终极权威是布鲁斯·威利斯，对吧？

897
00:34:19.700 --> 00:34:20.020
Yes.
是的。

898
00:34:20.440 --> 00:34:20.800
All right.
好吧。

899
00:34:20.980 --> 00:34:25.100
Well, Bruce Willis, he had his roast on Comedy Central.
布鲁斯·威利斯曾在喜剧中心参加过他的吐槽大会。

900
00:34:25.100 --> 00:34:27.380
He was roasted in 2018.
他在2018年被吐槽过。

901
00:34:27.800 --> 00:34:28.660
What did he say?
他说了什么？

902
00:34:28.660 --> 00:34:30.540
He addressed it at his roaSt.
他在吐槽大会上提到了这件事。

903
00:34:30.740 --> 00:34:32.020
Here's an audio clip.
这是音频片段。

904
00:34:32.860 --> 00:34:35.820
People ask me why I did this roaSt.
人们问我为什么要参加这次吐槽大会。

905
00:34:36.140 --> 00:34:40.100
Was it because one of the last guys who did it became president?
是因为上一位参加的人后来当了总统吗？

906
00:34:40.640 --> 00:34:41.220
Hell no.
见鬼，当然不是。

907
00:34:42.110 --> 00:34:47.140
Why would I want to be president when I can just keep being Bruce Willis?
既然能继续当布鲁斯·威利斯，我为什么要当总统呢？

908
00:34:51.110 --> 00:34:59.010
I did this roast for one reason and for one reason only to settle something once and for all.
我参加这次吐槽大会只有一个原因，而且是唯一的原因，就是为了彻底解决一件事。

909
00:34:59.610 --> 00:35:02.350
Now, please listen very carefully.
现在，请仔细听好。

910
00:35:02.350 --> 00:35:08.790
Seriously, Die Hard is not a Christmas movie.
说真的，《虎胆龙威》不是一部圣诞电影。

911
00:35:12.560 --> 00:35:15.320
It's a goddamn Bruce Willis movie.
它是一部该死的布鲁斯·威利斯电影。

912
00:35:19.380 --> 00:35:20.680
How about that?
怎么样？

913
00:35:21.100 --> 00:35:22.420
There you have it.
真相大白了。

914
00:35:22.540 --> 00:35:23.100
All right.
好吧。

915
00:35:23.400 --> 00:35:28.680
Well, in the kitchen, Jim is going to share with Stanley, Toby, and Creed about his new job in Philly.
在厨房里，吉姆正要和斯坦利、托比以及克里德分享他在费城的新工作。

916
00:35:29.300 --> 00:35:29.900
Daryl enters.
达里尔进来了。

917
00:35:30.180 --> 00:35:33.260
He's really happy for Jim, but he's like, hey, are you ready to go?
他真心为吉姆感到高兴，但他问，嘿，你准备好出发了吗？

918
00:35:33.420 --> 00:35:34.740
Do you have everything?
你东西都带齐了吗？

919
00:35:34.740 --> 00:35:36.200
Are you missing something?
你是不是落下了什么？

920
00:35:36.640 --> 00:35:37.060
Yeah.
是的。

921
00:35:37.220 --> 00:35:41.180
Then Daryl has a talking head where he says, Jim promised to take me to Philly.
然后达里尔有个单人访谈，他说，吉姆答应带我去费城。

922
00:35:41.180 --> 00:35:45.180
That was two months ago, and he hasn't heard anything since.
那是两个月前的事了，从那以后他就没再提过。

923
00:35:45.500 --> 00:35:46.700
He said that, right?
他确实这么说了，对吧？

924
00:35:47.000 --> 00:35:50.320
And we go back to the kitchen, and Jim is like, I don't think so.
我们回到厨房，吉姆却说，我不这么认为。

925
00:35:50.420 --> 00:35:51.420
I'm not forgetting anything.
我没落下任何东西。

926
00:35:51.760 --> 00:35:54.520
This is going to send Daryl on a journey.
这让达里尔踏上了一段旅程。

927
00:35:54.740 --> 00:35:56.020
A true spiral.
一段真正的心理崩溃之旅。

928
00:35:56.020 --> 00:35:56.700
A true spiral.
确实是崩溃。

929
00:35:56.700 --> 00:35:58.040
If there ever was one.
如果真有这种事的话。

930
00:35:58.720 --> 00:36:04.720
Toby, of course, relates everything back to his time as a juror on the Scranton Strangler trial.
托比当然把一切都联系到了他担任斯克兰顿勒杀手案陪审员的那段经历。

931
00:36:04.960 --> 00:36:06.700
This was like a huge moment for Toby.
这对托比来说是个极其重要的时刻。

932
00:36:07.040 --> 00:36:07.220
Yeah.
没错。

933
00:36:07.360 --> 00:36:09.080
It's like his one claim to fame.
这就像是他唯一值得吹嘘的事迹。

934
00:36:09.140 --> 00:36:09.680
It is.
确实。

935
00:36:09.740 --> 00:36:10.220
It is.
确实是。

936
00:36:10.320 --> 00:36:17.160
He points out that the man alleged to be the Scranton Strangler is someone who won't be working on anything new or exciting.
他指出，那个被指控为斯克兰顿勒杀手的人，以后不会再参与任何新鲜或刺激的事情了。

937
00:36:17.620 --> 00:36:20.100
He's in prison for something he may not have done.
他因为一件可能没做过的事被关在监狱里。

938
00:36:20.540 --> 00:36:21.180
Oh, no.
噢，不。

939
00:36:21.860 --> 00:36:22.640
Nellie's like, what?
奈莉一脸茫然，什么？

940
00:36:22.760 --> 00:36:23.440
What are you talking about?
你在说什么？

941
00:36:23.580 --> 00:36:24.420
The Scranton who?
斯克兰顿什么？

942
00:36:24.700 --> 00:36:25.220
Oh, no.
噢，不。

943
00:36:25.440 --> 00:36:25.880
Oh, boy.
天哪。

944
00:36:26.080 --> 00:36:26.240
Yep.
没错。

945
00:36:26.640 --> 00:36:27.420
Toby lights up.
托比兴奋起来了。

946
00:36:27.540 --> 00:36:28.180
He's so excited.
他太激动了。

947
00:36:28.320 --> 00:36:30.320
He has someone new to share this whole story with.
他终于有新人可以分享他那整套故事了。

948
00:36:30.880 --> 00:36:35.320
How much did you love John and Craig's exit from the kitchen?
你有多喜欢约翰和克雷格离开厨房的那一幕？

949
00:36:35.620 --> 00:36:36.320
So great.
太棒了。

950
00:36:36.520 --> 00:36:37.860
I love Stanley's exit, too.
我也很喜欢斯坦利离开的方式。

951
00:36:37.940 --> 00:36:38.640
He's like, all right.
他当时就说，行吧。

952
00:36:38.880 --> 00:36:39.320
See you.
回见。

953
00:36:39.640 --> 00:36:40.660
Good luck with that.
祝你好运。

954
00:36:40.660 --> 00:36:42.040
Yes, see you in a few hours.
好的，几个小时后见。

955
00:36:42.280 --> 00:36:42.360
Yep.
没错。

956
00:36:43.580 --> 00:36:47.040
I want to point out the background of this scene.
我想指出一下这个场景的背景。

957
00:36:47.220 --> 00:36:56.080
This is a very good example of how during our entire nine years on this show, we were always doing background work for other actors' scenes.
这是一个很好的例子，说明在我们拍摄这部剧的九年里，我们一直都在为其他演员的戏份做背景表演。

958
00:36:56.400 --> 00:37:00.700
Did you notice Aaron and Pete are in the background?
你们注意到亚伦和皮特在背景里了吗？

959
00:37:00.940 --> 00:37:08.460
And Pete is actively reciting Die Hard to Aaron all throughout this entire scene.
皮特在整个场景中都在给亚伦背诵《虎胆龙威》的台词。

960
00:37:08.600 --> 00:37:09.660
They're just in the background.
他们就在背景里。

961
00:37:09.780 --> 00:37:10.380
You can't hear them.
你听不见他们说话。

962
00:37:10.380 --> 00:37:12.580
You can barely see them, but you can see him moving.
你几乎看不清他们，但能看到他在动。

963
00:37:13.660 --> 00:37:15.400
Great background acting commitment.
非常敬业的背景表演。

964
00:37:15.760 --> 00:37:20.040
I mean, probably three hours they spent in the background while we did this kitchen scene.
我是说，在我们拍这场厨房戏的时候，他们大概在背景里待了三个小时。

965
00:37:20.240 --> 00:37:20.560
Yep.
没错。

966
00:37:20.760 --> 00:37:21.060
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

967
00:37:21.600 --> 00:37:28.640
Back at Angela's party planning committee meeting, Pam is really trying to make a case for Dwight's Christmas.
回到安吉拉的派对策划委员会会议上，帕姆真的在努力争取举办德怀特圣诞派对。

968
00:37:29.040 --> 00:37:29.340
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

969
00:37:30.180 --> 00:37:30.520
Yeah.
是啊。

970
00:37:31.360 --> 00:37:32.580
And guess what?
你猜怎么着？

971
00:37:32.740 --> 00:37:34.040
She gets everyone on board.
她让所有人都同意了。

972
00:37:34.240 --> 00:37:35.240
Everyone but Angela.
除了安吉拉。

973
00:37:35.400 --> 00:37:37.100
Angela does not want her name on this.
安吉拉不想让自己的名字出现在上面。

974
00:37:37.260 --> 00:37:38.460
I love this so much.
我太喜欢这一段了。

975
00:37:38.460 --> 00:37:41.180
She was like, please do not attach my name to this.
她说，请别把我的名字加在上面。

976
00:37:41.280 --> 00:37:42.340
And Pam's like, where?
帕姆就问，哪里？

977
00:37:42.480 --> 00:37:43.540
Where is your name going to appear?
你的名字会出现在哪里？

978
00:37:43.700 --> 00:37:45.940
And Oscar's like, just take her name off of it.
奥斯卡就说，直接把她的名字删掉就行了。

979
00:37:45.940 --> 00:37:46.360
I know.
我知道。

980
00:37:46.540 --> 00:37:48.040
I love Oscar in that moment.
我喜欢那一刻的奥斯卡。

981
00:37:48.540 --> 00:37:55.620
So the PPC emerged from the conference room to announce we are doing Dwight's Christmas.
所以派对策划委员会从会议室出来，宣布我们要举办德怀特圣诞派对了。

982
00:37:55.860 --> 00:37:57.340
But there is a rule.
但有一条规则。

983
00:37:57.560 --> 00:38:00.780
The one rule is there are no rules.
唯一的规则就是没有规则。

984
00:38:00.780 --> 00:38:03.100
Dwight's like, you have never been cooler.
德怀特当时觉得，你们真是太酷了。

985
00:38:03.680 --> 00:38:05.760
I mean, Pam has made his day.
我是说，帕姆让他这一天过得太开心了。

986
00:38:05.980 --> 00:38:06.880
Jim applauds.
吉姆鼓掌。

987
00:38:07.140 --> 00:38:07.900
He's so happy.
他太高兴了。

988
00:38:08.360 --> 00:38:09.660
Best Christmas ever.
这是最棒的圣诞节。

989
00:38:10.340 --> 00:38:15.080
So we reached out to Rainn Wilson about this episode, and he sent in some audio clips.
所以我们联系了雷恩·威尔森聊了聊这一集，他发来了一些音频片段。

990
00:38:15.260 --> 00:38:22.440
In the first one, he shares with us about working with Charles McDougal and also how this idea had been around for a long time.
在第一段里，他分享了与查尔斯·麦克杜格尔合作的经历，以及这个点子是如何酝酿已久的。

991
00:38:23.580 --> 00:38:26.520
Hello, office ladies, and here's your old friend, Rainn Wilson.
你好，办公室女士们，我是你们的老朋友，雷恩·威尔森。

992
00:38:26.980 --> 00:38:30.820
And what an honor and pleasure it was to go back and watch Dwight Christmas.
能回过头来重温《德怀特圣诞》真是我的荣幸和乐事。

993
00:38:31.000 --> 00:38:36.160
I don't think I had seen it since it first came out 10 years ago, 11 years ago, something like that.
我想自它十年前、十一年年前左右首播以来，我就没再看过。

994
00:38:36.640 --> 00:38:38.580
It was so much fun to watch.
看的时候真的很有趣。

995
00:38:38.660 --> 00:38:40.820
It brought so many memories back.
它勾起了我许多回忆。

996
00:38:41.060 --> 00:38:43.440
I had such a great time shooting it.
拍摄的时候我玩得很开心。

997
00:38:43.440 --> 00:38:50.100
The director of that episode was the famous Charles McDougal, who would always do 47 takes with camera angles.
那一集的导演是著名的查尔斯·麦克杜格尔，他总是会用不同的摄像机角度拍上47条。

998
00:38:50.200 --> 00:38:54.360
For those of you keeping track, like, watch how many different places the cameras are in,
对于那些在留心观察的人，你们可以看看摄像机出现在多少个不同的位置，

999
00:38:54.440 --> 00:39:02.520
and that there is no possible way in heaven that this is a mockumentary with two cameras wandering around an office capturing things.
而且根本不可能这是一部由两台摄像机在办公室里四处游走捕捉画面的伪纪录片。

1000
00:39:02.640 --> 00:39:06.520
But we had long let go of that conceit by season nine.
但到了第九季，我们早就放弃了那种设定。

1001
00:39:07.080 --> 00:39:12.980
I know that Justin Spitzer had been wanting to do this Belschnickel thing for a long time.
我知道贾斯汀·斯皮策一直想做这个贝尔斯尼克尔的桥段，已经想了很久了。

1002
00:39:12.980 --> 00:39:16.200
They'd been trying to figure out an episode for it.
他们一直在想怎么把它写进剧集里。

1003
00:39:16.320 --> 00:39:21.400
I think he had come up with the idea and the research and was very excited about it.
我想他当时已经构思好了点子，也做了调研，对此非常兴奋。

1004
00:39:22.340 --> 00:39:23.480
Yeah, you know what?
是啊，你知道吗？

1005
00:39:23.480 --> 00:39:24.460
I remember that.
我记得那件事。

1006
00:39:24.660 --> 00:39:32.880
I think this episode of Dwight hosting the Christmas was supposed to happen during the year of the strike.
我觉得德怀特主持圣诞节的那一集，本该是在罢工那一年播出的。

1007
00:39:33.400 --> 00:39:37.280
I do sort of vaguely remember, like, it was a card on the wall, right?
我隐约记得，当时墙上的卡片上写着这个，对吧？

1008
00:39:37.380 --> 00:39:37.520
Yes, yes.
没错，没错。

1009
00:39:37.520 --> 00:39:38.940
And they were working towards it.
他们当时正朝着这个方向努力。

1010
00:39:39.060 --> 00:39:42.280
Yeah, but then we did not end up having a Christmas episode that year.
是啊，但后来那一年我们没能拍成圣诞特辑。

1011
00:39:42.280 --> 00:39:45.640
And so I think it had been on the shelf ever since then.
所以我猜从那以后，这个点子就一直被搁置了。

1012
00:39:45.980 --> 00:39:50.900
Well, I guess Dwight just keeps a horn laying around because he's going to blow this horn.
好吧，我猜德怀特随身带着号角，因为他打算吹响它。

1013
00:39:51.340 --> 00:39:53.780
Pennsylvania Dutch Christmas has officially begun.
宾夕法尼亚荷兰式圣诞节正式开始。

1014
00:39:54.240 --> 00:39:57.820
He immediately already has a spread of food and wine.
他立刻就摆出了一大桌食物和葡萄酒。

1015
00:39:58.000 --> 00:39:59.900
I don't know how he threw this together.
我不知道他是怎么这么快准备好的。

1016
00:40:00.140 --> 00:40:01.380
He was ready to go.
他早就准备好了。

1017
00:40:02.200 --> 00:40:04.560
Meredith is going to take a sip of the glow wine,
梅雷迪思要喝一口热红酒，

1018
00:40:04.940 --> 00:40:09.460
and people are, like, really not really loving the glow wine.
大家好像真的不太喜欢这热红酒。

1019
00:40:09.460 --> 00:40:10.840
It's very thick.
它太浓稠了。

1020
00:40:10.900 --> 00:40:12.800
She says, is this lava?
她说，这是岩浆吗？

1021
00:40:13.180 --> 00:40:16.260
I want you to know, I looked up glow wine recipes.
我想让你知道，我查过热红酒的食谱。

1022
00:40:17.060 --> 00:40:19.020
You didn't make it, did you?
你没亲手做吧？

1023
00:40:19.460 --> 00:40:20.520
Josh made it.
是乔希做的。

1024
00:40:21.140 --> 00:40:22.320
Is it here?
它在这儿吗？

1025
00:40:22.560 --> 00:40:22.920
Yes.
在的。

1026
00:40:23.300 --> 00:40:24.140
Dear God.
天哪。

1027
00:40:24.600 --> 00:40:26.000
But wait, listen.
等等，听着。

1028
00:40:26.000 --> 00:40:26.880
Oh, my God.
天哪。

1029
00:40:27.000 --> 00:40:27.740
Listen to this.
听听这个。

1030
00:40:27.780 --> 00:40:28.340
I'm scared.
我好怕。

1031
00:40:28.600 --> 00:40:30.100
No, do not be scared.
不，别怕。

1032
00:40:30.500 --> 00:40:31.800
Have you tried it yet?
你尝过了吗？

1033
00:40:31.980 --> 00:40:34.680
No, I wanted to try it the same time you tried it.
还没，我想和你一起尝。

1034
00:40:34.780 --> 00:40:35.300
Oh, my God.
天哪。

1035
00:40:35.300 --> 00:40:39.200
Here, I want you to know, I found this recipe on allrecipes.com.
来，我想让你知道，我是在allrecipes.com上找到这个食谱的。

1036
00:40:39.360 --> 00:40:39.620
Okay.
好吧。

1037
00:40:40.160 --> 00:40:46.140
Glow wine is a hot, spiced, quote, glow wine found in many winter markets in Germany and Austria.
热红酒是一种热的、加了香料的，所谓的热红酒，在德国和奥地利的许多冬季市场上都能见到。

1038
00:40:46.500 --> 00:40:47.660
And you know what?
你知道吗？

1039
00:40:47.780 --> 00:40:56.020
You come in from the cold and snow, and this warm, spiced, mulled drink is supposed to make you glow with warmth inside.
当你从寒风雪地里走进来，喝上一杯这种温暖、辛香的热饮，整个人都会从内而外地暖和起来。

1040
00:40:56.560 --> 00:40:58.380
This recipe is from Elsie.
这个食谱是埃尔西提供的。

1041
00:40:58.600 --> 00:41:02.120
Elsie says, my father would make this for New Year's Eve.
埃尔西说，她父亲以前会在除夕夜做这个。

1042
00:41:02.120 --> 00:41:05.520
Listen to the ingredients before you get scared, okay?
在你害怕之前，先听听配料表，好吗？

1043
00:41:05.580 --> 00:41:06.660
Okay, okay, okay.
好吧，好吧，好吧。

1044
00:41:06.840 --> 00:41:09.980
I'm just saying the visual in the episode is not appealing.
我只是说剧里的视觉效果看起来不太诱人。

1045
00:41:10.160 --> 00:41:11.160
I know, that's right.
我知道，确实如此。

1046
00:41:11.240 --> 00:41:14.340
But now I'm hearing that it's meant to be, it's like a mulled wine.
但现在我听说它本该就是那样的，就像热红酒一样。

1047
00:41:14.340 --> 00:41:15.840
It's like served warm.
它是热着喝的。

1048
00:41:16.200 --> 00:41:19.940
I felt like I had to find out, is glow wine a real thing?
我当时觉得我必须弄清楚，热红酒是真的吗？

1049
00:41:20.020 --> 00:41:20.520
Is it gross?
它很难喝吗？

1050
00:41:20.520 --> 00:41:21.080
Is it not?
还是说其实不然？

1051
00:41:21.180 --> 00:41:23.120
And it sounds lovely, and it is a real thing.
听起来很棒，而且这确实是真实存在的东西。

1052
00:41:23.360 --> 00:41:30.040
The ingredients are water, sugar, cinnamon stick, oranges, cloves, and a bottle of red wine.
配料有水、糖、肉桂棒、橙子、丁香和一瓶红酒。

1053
00:41:30.180 --> 00:41:31.280
And you cook it up.
然后把它煮开。

1054
00:41:31.280 --> 00:41:32.220
Oh, that sounds delicious.
噢，听起来真美味。

1055
00:41:32.480 --> 00:41:34.200
I know, you cook it up and serve it hot.
我知道，煮好后趁热喝。

1056
00:41:34.380 --> 00:41:39.280
And I was going to make it last night, but I was making Sam's scrapbook.
我本来昨晚想做的，但当时在忙着做萨姆的剪贴簿。

1057
00:41:39.460 --> 00:41:39.680
Yes.
是的。

1058
00:41:39.840 --> 00:41:41.440
And Josh was like, babe, I'll make it for you.
乔什就说，宝贝，我来给你做。

1059
00:41:41.660 --> 00:41:46.800
So he made it, and I have it here, and we're going to try some glue wine.
所以他做了，我现在带过来了，我们要尝尝这热红酒。

1060
00:41:47.080 --> 00:41:47.600
All right.
好的。

1061
00:41:48.020 --> 00:41:53.900
So you get a little orange garnish, and you, these oranges were from my tree.
你可以加一点橙子装饰，这些橙子是我树上摘的。

1062
00:41:54.900 --> 00:41:57.360
Wow, this, I mean, now I'm excited.
哇，这个，我是说，我现在很兴奋。

1063
00:41:57.720 --> 00:41:58.180
I know.
我知道。

1064
00:41:58.600 --> 00:42:01.040
It's not as thick as what we had on set.
它不像我们在片场喝的那种那么浓稠。

1065
00:42:01.580 --> 00:42:02.360
Or is it?
或者说，是吗？

1066
00:42:02.500 --> 00:42:02.560
No.
不是。

1067
00:42:02.560 --> 00:42:03.220
We don't know yet.
我们还不知道。

1068
00:42:03.260 --> 00:42:04.200
I don't know.
我不知道。

1069
00:42:04.360 --> 00:42:05.120
I doubt it.
我怀疑不是。

1070
00:42:05.680 --> 00:42:10.380
And it's also not being served with the spoon that guided your head through the birth canal.
而且它也不是用那种引导你头穿过产道的勺子盛出来的。

1071
00:42:10.780 --> 00:42:11.060
Exactly.
没错。

1072
00:42:11.460 --> 00:42:14.200
And also, it's supposed to be served warm, because, you know.
而且，它应该趁热喝，因为，你知道的。

1073
00:42:14.260 --> 00:42:15.000
Oh, it's steaming.
噢，它在冒热气呢。

1074
00:42:15.280 --> 00:42:20.940
These are cold, you know, you're, and a lot of, I guess, tourists like to get it after they ski.
这些是冷的，你知道，而且我想很多游客喜欢滑完雪后喝这个。

1075
00:42:21.420 --> 00:42:23.960
Oh, well, now you're speaking my language, Angela.
噢，好吧，安吉拉，你现在说到我心坎里去了。

1076
00:42:24.340 --> 00:42:24.740
I know.
我知道。

1077
00:42:25.620 --> 00:42:26.140
Okay.
好的。

1078
00:42:26.440 --> 00:42:27.460
Here you go.
给你。

1079
00:42:27.620 --> 00:42:28.840
Thank you so much.
太感谢你了。

1080
00:42:29.080 --> 00:42:30.900
Let's enjoy your glue wine.
让我们享受你的热红酒吧。

1081
00:42:31.200 --> 00:42:33.940
It smells good, and I'm imagining that I'm chilly.
闻起来很香，我正在想象自己感到寒冷。

1082
00:42:34.360 --> 00:42:34.820
I'm cold.
我很冷。

1083
00:42:34.920 --> 00:42:37.180
Oh, I even have snow on my hair.
噢，我头发上甚至还有雪。

1084
00:42:37.200 --> 00:42:37.920
Oh, my gosh.
天哪。

1085
00:42:40.820 --> 00:42:43.120
Oh, it's fantastic.
噢，太棒了。

1086
00:42:44.260 --> 00:42:45.180
That is wonderful.
这真是太美妙了。

1087
00:42:45.780 --> 00:42:46.560
It's real good.
真的很好喝。

1088
00:42:46.740 --> 00:42:47.420
It's real good.
真的很好喝。

1089
00:42:47.840 --> 00:42:48.680
Josh did great.
乔什做得太棒了。

1090
00:42:48.820 --> 00:42:49.320
I know.
我知道。

1091
00:42:49.340 --> 00:42:50.180
He's good.
他很厉害。

1092
00:42:51.100 --> 00:42:56.560
It literally means to light you from within, like to warm you up.
它字面意思是从内部点亮你，就像让你暖和起来一样。

1093
00:42:56.800 --> 00:42:57.680
To glow you up.
让你由内而外地发光。

1094
00:42:57.900 --> 00:42:58.860
Lit from within.
由内而外地照亮。

1095
00:42:59.300 --> 00:43:01.960
Well, Angela, I'm really glad you did that, and thank you, Josh.
好吧，安吉拉，我真的很高兴你做了这个，也谢谢你，乔什。

1096
00:43:02.240 --> 00:43:02.800
I know.
我知道。

1097
00:43:03.040 --> 00:43:03.740
It's delicious.
太美味了。

1098
00:43:03.920 --> 00:43:05.520
It is really good, isn't it?
真的很好喝，不是吗？

1099
00:43:05.640 --> 00:43:11.920
We also, we got a fan mail flurry asking what parts of Dwight's Christmas are based in fact.
我们还收到了一大波粉丝来信，问《德怀特的圣诞节》里哪些部分是基于事实的。

1100
00:43:12.360 --> 00:43:15.680
Oh, I bet, because there's a lot of random stuff he's sharing.
噢，我敢肯定，因为他分享了很多乱七八糟的东西。

1101
00:43:15.960 --> 00:43:20.160
Yes, and writer Robert Padnick said that there wasn't actually a lot of
没错，编剧罗伯特·帕德尼克说其实并没有太多

1102
00:43:20.160 --> 00:43:26.140
information about a Pennsylvania Dutch Christmas, or Belschnickel, who we'll be meeting in a minute,
关于宾夕法尼亚荷兰人圣诞节，或者说我们一会儿要见到的贝尔施尼克尔的信息，

1103
00:43:26.360 --> 00:43:28.880
that was kind of out on the internet at the time.
当时在互联网上几乎找不到相关资料。

1104
00:43:29.060 --> 00:43:32.360
But they were very careful to not make anything up.
但他们非常谨慎，没有编造任何内容。

1105
00:43:32.760 --> 00:43:37.600
He said that our writers Jonathan Green and Gabe Miller did a lot of work on this episode
他说我们的编剧乔纳森·格林和盖比·米勒为这一集做了大量工作，

1106
00:43:37.600 --> 00:43:40.060
and included a number of real traditions.
并加入了一些真实的传统习俗。

1107
00:43:40.060 --> 00:43:43.700
We also got a fan letter from Andreas H.
我们还收到了一封来自德国安德烈亚斯·H的粉丝来信，

1108
00:43:43.900 --> 00:43:46.340
in Germany, who said,
他在信中说：

1109
00:43:47.700 --> 00:43:48.940
Hi, office ladies.
嗨，办公室女士们。

1110
00:43:49.580 --> 00:43:53.860
This episode calls for a deep dive into German Christmas traditions,
这一集需要深入探讨德国的圣诞传统，

1111
00:43:53.860 --> 00:43:56.600
and since I am from Germany and I love Christmas,
既然我来自德国，而且我热爱圣诞节，

1112
00:43:56.920 --> 00:43:59.980
I took the liberty of assisting you in your research.
我就自作主张帮你们做了一些研究。

1113
00:44:00.300 --> 00:44:01.380
Oh my gosh, awesome.
天哪，太棒了。

1114
00:44:01.740 --> 00:44:03.320
Andreas said, though,
不过安德烈亚斯说，

1115
00:44:03.320 --> 00:44:07.940
So, beware, this will take some time and some weird turns.
所以，要小心了，这会花点时间，而且会变得有些奇怪。

1116
00:44:08.500 --> 00:44:08.660
Oh.
噢。

1117
00:44:09.440 --> 00:44:13.300
Andreas said, let's break down the props and decorations firSt.
安德烈亚斯说，我们先来拆解一下道具和装饰吧。

1118
00:44:13.780 --> 00:44:18.940
Andreas, I'm loving everything about this as I sip my glue wine and listen.
安德烈亚斯，我一边喝着热红酒一边听，简直爱死这些内容了。

1119
00:44:19.160 --> 00:44:20.080
I know, isn't this perfect?
我知道，这太完美了不是吗？

1120
00:44:20.280 --> 00:44:20.600
Yeah.
是啊。

1121
00:44:20.860 --> 00:44:26.760
So, the first thing that Andreas pointed out was the starry light thing above reception,
所以，安德烈亚斯指出的第一件事就是接待处上方那个星形的灯，

1122
00:44:27.240 --> 00:44:31.260
which, Angela, you know we called the Death Star.
安吉拉，你知道我们管它叫死星。

1123
00:44:31.260 --> 00:44:32.960
We did call it the Death Star.
我们确实管它叫死星。

1124
00:44:33.140 --> 00:44:34.940
This is not a reference to Star Wars.
这并不是在致敬《星球大战》。

1125
00:44:34.940 --> 00:44:37.660
It's just the fact that it was really pointy and sharp,
只是因为它真的很尖锐，

1126
00:44:37.660 --> 00:44:40.420
and several people walked into it and got injured.
好几个人撞上去受了伤。

1127
00:44:40.840 --> 00:44:41.520
They did.
确实撞了。

1128
00:44:41.680 --> 00:44:45.420
And then, like, midway through the first day,
然后，大概在第一天过了一半的时候，

1129
00:44:45.520 --> 00:44:46.840
there had been so many injuries.
已经发生了太多起受伤事件。

1130
00:44:46.840 --> 00:44:53.340
It was hung so low by reception that they put corks on the end of all the points,
它在接待处挂得太低了，以至于他们不得不给所有的尖角都套上软木塞，

1131
00:44:53.340 --> 00:44:55.860
and they draped it in, like, caution tape.
还给它缠上了警戒线。

1132
00:44:55.860 --> 00:44:56.400
Caution tape.
警戒线。

1133
00:44:56.660 --> 00:44:58.820
So many people walked into this thing.
太多人撞到这东西了。

1134
00:44:58.980 --> 00:45:00.320
Someone cut their forehead, remember?
有人额头被划破了，还记得吗？

1135
00:45:00.320 --> 00:45:03.320
Yeah, I can't remember who that was, but more than one person.
记得，我不记得是谁了，但受伤的不止一个人。

1136
00:45:03.580 --> 00:45:04.240
More than one person.
不止一个人。

1137
00:45:04.240 --> 00:45:07.540
And who knew we were going to have to have a safety meeting about this prop?
谁能想到我们竟然得为这个道具专门开个安全会议？

1138
00:45:07.900 --> 00:45:08.260
Yes.
